# =============================================================================
# excludes.local -- THIS host's exclude patterns  (SAMPLE / template)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#     cp excludes.local.sample /root/.config/restic/excludes.local   # then edit
#
# Hand-managed, per host, like `config`, `encryption-pw` and `pre-backup`.
# deploy.sh NEVER touches it. The file is optional -- with no excludes.local at
# all the host just gets the shared `excludes`, which is the normal case.
#
# Read AFTER the shared `excludes`, and that order is the whole point: a later
# pattern beats an earlier one, so this file can both ADD exclusions and TAKE
# BACK one the fleet-wide file made.
#
#   !!! Same comment rule as `excludes`: restic treats a line as a comment ONLY
#   !!! when "#" is the FIRST character. An inline comment becomes part of the
#   !!! pattern and then silently matches nothing.
#
# You cannot re-include the encryption password or config: restic-backup.sh
# excludes those two from $CONFIG_DIR on the command line, by design.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Taking a shared exclusion BACK (prefix "!") ----------------------------
# On a production host a restore that already contains the dependency tree is
# deterministic and needs no network. The shared file excludes these; undo it
# here, for this host only:
# !.venv
# !venv
# !vendor

# ---- Extra paths only this host has ----------------------------------------
# Anchored at the backup root (BACKUP_PATHS=(/) => the real absolute path).
# /srv/scratch
# /var/lib/myapp/cache

# ---- .NET build output, anchored so bare "obj" cannot hit /usr/bin etc. -----
# /home/user/code/**/obj
# /home/user/code/**/bin

# ---- A DB volume you already capture as a consistent dump ------------------
# The live copy under /var/lib/docker/volumes is torn; the dump is the source of
# truth, so the redundant copy can go:
# /var/lib/docker/volumes/myapp_db
